      "overviewText": "If you’ve ever thought of visiting Thailand, this is **THE time to do it.**\n\nWelcome to the Thailand Community Trip – Songkran Edition, a 6 days 5 nights experience that combines Thailand’s biggest festival + island life + community travel vibes all in one perfectly curated trip from India.\n\nThis isn’t your typical Thailand itinerary. This is where you’re **celebrating Songkran on the streets of [Phuket](https://indiatour.live/attractions/phuket), partying at Bangla Road, hopping across Phi Phi Islands, and unwinding in the tropical beauty of [Krabi](https://indiatour.live/attractions/krabi)** all while travelling with a like-minded group.\n\n### **What is Songkran Festival?**\n\n**Songkran Festival** marks the **Thai New Year**, celebrated every year from **13th to 15th April** across Thailand. Rooted in tradition, it symbolises **cleansing, renewal, and fresh beginnings**.\n\nTraditionally, locals visit temples, offer prayers, and gently pour water over Buddha statues and elders’ hands as a sign of respect and to wash away the past year’s negativity.\n\nBut over time, Songkran has evolved into something much bigger.\n\nToday, it’s known as the **world’s largest water festival**, where entire cities transform into vibrant celebration zones. Streets are filled with people splashing water, music playing on every corner, and an atmosphere that’s equal parts cultural and high-energy.\n\nFor travellers, Songkran is not just a festival you watch it’s one you **become a part of**, experiencing [Thailand](https://indiatour.live/thailand) at its most lively, joyful, and unforgettable.\n\nStart planning your [Songkran trip](https://indiatour.live/thailand) here!\n\n### What makes this Thailand trip different?\n\n**1. Celebrate Songkran in Phuket (Peak Experience):** \nExperience Thailand’s most iconic festival in its full glory. **Songkran** isn’t just a celebration it’s a cultural reset, where water symbolizes cleansing and new beginnings. But on the streets? It’s the **world’s biggest water fight**. Expect high-energy crowds, live music, street parties, and moments that turn complete strangers into your festival crew.\n\n**2. Explore Thailand’s most iconic islands:** \nThis trip takes you beyond the mainland into Thailand’s postcard-perfect landscapes. Cruise through the turquoise waters of the **[Phi Phi Islands](https://indiatour.live/attractions/phi-phi-island) on a speedboat**, witness dramatic limestone cliffs, hidden lagoons, and vibrant marine life, and then experience the charm of Krabi with a **4-island longtail boat tour** a slower, more scenic side of Thailand.\n\n**3. Perfect mix of party & paradise:** \nOne moment you’re in the heart of **Bangla Street’s nightlife**, surrounded by neon lights and music, and the next you’re floating in the middle of the Andaman Sea, surrounded by untouched beauty. This balance of **high-energy experiences and laid-back island moments** is what makes this trip unforgettable.\n\n**4. Community travel, not a typical group tour:** \nThis is not about following a flag and ticking destinations off a list. It’s about travelling with a group that feels like your vibe people who want to **celebrate, explore, and genuinely enjoy the journey**. Expect shared moments, spontaneous plans, and connections that go beyond the trip.\n\n**5. Curated for Indian travellers:** \nFrom **comfortable stays in Phuket, Phi Phi, and [Krabi](https://indiatour.live/attractions/krabi)** to seamless transfers, guided experiences, and on-ground support everything is designed to make your international travel smooth and stress-free. You don’t worry about the logistics, you just focus on living the experience.\n\nBook your [Songkran Trip to Thailand](https://indiatour.live/thailand) today!",
